           <li>Everything is counted in <strong>wins</strong>, using Ledger WAR, this project's own wins-above-replacement measure built from public MLB data. <strong>+2.0 WAR</strong> means two more team wins than a freely available player.</li>
           <li>A decision's <strong>+/-</strong> is what the club got against what a typical front office gets from the same move: a trade at +3.0 brought back three more wins than it gave up; a signing at −2.0 delivered two fewer wins than its price usually buys.</li>
